From 40f03baeac10d011415796bbdaf6feb9602105f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: paleluna82-del <260293746+paleluna82-del@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:58:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] CUDA/HIP: banded relative-bias attention on AMD WMMA via
 the MMA kernel

- ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_banded_use_mma: also on AMD RDNA (WMMA) when the GQA layout gives ncols2 >= 2
  (mask without head dim, n_kv % FATTN_KQ_STRIDE == 0, aligned strides). GGML_CUDA_BANDED_AMD_MMA=0 opts out.
- per-query sinks for the banded MMA path: launch_fattn appends a dense [n_seq, n_q, n_head] sink block
  after rel in a pool buffer and tags it with m1 = 2; the kernel reads sink per (query, head).
- test-backend-ops: Inkling-2-Mini shapes (GQA 24/8, n_kv 1536/8704, odd n_q, Q8_0 cache) in eval and perf.
- GGML_CUDA_BANDED_DEBUG_NOREL=1 drops rel and sinks for timing only (to be removed before sharing).

R9700 (gfx1201), Inkling-2-Mini UD-Q4_K_M, q8_0 KV, ROCBLAS_USE_HIPBLASLT=0:
pp512 1481 / pp2048 1241 / pp8192 951 / pp16384 900 / tg128 37.7
(scalar banded: 1019 / 700 / 546 / 400; Unsloth b12588 prebuilt: 1360 / 1087 / 867 / 735 / 35.8)
PPL c512 b512 x40 6.7326 (scalar 6.7402), c16384 b512 x2 5.0015 (5.0034), greedy 128 tokens identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
