From 94fa080ea6c066b6ebaddf71676e2044c1298f35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: paleluna82-del <260293746+paleluna82-del@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:58:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] inkling2: banded attention over a wrapped (ring) SWA
 cache

Once a sequence outgrows the SWA cache (n_swa + n_ubatch cells), position p lives in cell p % size and
get_n_kv_pos_contiguous returned 0, so the 40 SWA layer applications fell back to the dense relative bias.

- llama_kv_cache::get_n_kv_pos_ring: accepts a full ring (each of the last size positions in cell pos % size,
  the ubatch is the newest tail) and returns the rotation (cell of the oldest position); dense otherwise.
- ggml_flash_attn_ext_banded_set_kv_rot (op_params i32 slot 6): the relative distance uses the logical index
  (cell - rot) mod n_kv. CPU reference and the CUDA/HIP MMA kernel implement it (rotation passed in m0);
  every other banded kernel rejects a nonzero rotation, and the model probes support with one, so it falls
  back to dense. Rotation is part of the graph-reuse check.
- test-backend-ops: rotations 1/511/1024/1535/700, F16 and Q8_0 caches, per-head and per-query sinks.

R9700, UD-Q4_K_M, q8_0 KV, ROCBLAS_USE_HIPBLASLT_BATCHED=0:
pp512 1518 / pp2048 1458 / pp8192 1413 / pp16384 1371 / pp32768 1308 / tg128 37.4
(before: 1481 / 1241 / 951 / 900; Unsloth b12588 prebuilt: 1363 / 1086 / 865 / 735 / 570 / 35.8)
All 48 layer applications banded in every ubatch of a 3.3K prompt. PPL c512 b512 x40 6.7313 (dense 6.7333),
c16384 b512 x2 4.9991 (5.0027); greedy output on a ~2K-token prompt identical to the dense path.

