From 4bf7eed705493e149cbad6550448a5592504cbf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: paleluna82-del <260293746+paleluna82-del@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:58:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] inkling2: pad an unrotated banded K/V cell count to the
 FA KV stride

A contiguous full-attention cache has exactly pos_max + 1 cells, so a decode-sized append (e.g. 128 tokens at
depth 13312) gave n_kv % 256 != 0 and the WMMA banded path fell back to the scalar kernel (7 ms per call).
Pad to a multiple of 256 within the mask width and express the offset as a rotation of n (logical index
(cell - n) mod n_pad), so the queries stay aligned to the tail of the real cells; the padded cells hold no
position of the sequence and are masked. Backends without rotated banded attention keep the unpadded layout.
The graph-reuse check compares the cache's raw (n, rot) and the mask width.

R9700: pp128 @ d13312 234 -> 654 t/s, pp300 @ d13312 943, pp512 @ d13312 1387 (Unsloth b12588: 475 / - / 602).
PPL c640 b512 x30 6.3401 (dense 6.3415). Greedy on a 2242-token prompt matches the dense path until a near-tie
(7.85% vs 7.32% top-2) at token 36.

