Subject: [PATCH 5/8] inkling2 : fuse short-conv residual and loop-controller
 gate on CUDA/HIP

Decode on this model is bound by the number of small kernels (~5600 per
token), and each tiny elementwise kernel costs ~2.2 us inside a HIP graph.

- ssm_conv: optionally fuse a residual add and a scale,
  (res + conv(x, w))*s, as SSM_CONV -> ADD -> SCALE. inkling2 builds the
  non-dynamic short convolutions in that order (192 per token).
- new fused tanh gate mix, (x - tanh(f)*x) + tanh(g)*m, for the
  UNARY(TANH) -> MUL -> SUB -> UNARY(TANH) -> MUL -> ADD subgraph of the
  loop controllers. inkling2 expands the projections and the message
  first so that the elementwise tail is contiguous.
- test-backend-ops cases for both.

R9700, Q4_K_M, q8_0 KV, with #400-#402 applied: tg128 41.8 -> 45.8 t/s, pp512 1519 -> 1559.
PPL unchanged at c512 (7.6923 -> 7.6899), KLD 0.001 vs the unfused path.

