From 502842e1da62a0584e0dd7f5c850dfa404f41fe8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: paleluna82-del <260293746+paleluna82-del@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:05:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] inkling2 : fuse the short-conv input concat and state
 store into the conv on CUDA/HIP

Each non-dynamic short convolution concatenates the past columns from the
recurrent state with the new inputs, copies the last columns back to the
state, convolves, adds the residual and scales: five kernels, 192 times
per token. Fuse CONCAT -> VIEW -> VIEW -> CPY -> SSM_CONV -> ADD -> SCALE
into one kernel that reads the past from the state, keeps the window in
registers and writes the new past back (n_t <= 32, d_conv 4). inkling2
expands the conv output right after the state store so that the nodes are
adjacent. Disable with GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_SSM_CONV_HIST_FUSION.

R9700, Q4_K_M, q8_0 KV, with #400-#402 applied: tg128 45.8 -> 47.5 t/s. KLD vs unfused 0.000000
(max 5.6e-5) with ubatch 16 and with 4 sequences per ubatch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
