From c389899fe4d8e1e7c387c160aae637e9287fd5bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: paleluna82-del <260293746+paleluna82-del@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:10:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] CUDA/HIP : reuse the q8_1 src1 of mul_mat_vec_q across
 products of the same input

Several projections of one input (Q, rel, sink, gate, ...) each quantized
the same src1 to q8_1 again: 385 quantize kernels per token on
Inkling-2-Mini decode for ~290 products. Keep the q8_1 copy of the last
mul_mat_vec_q src1 in a per-context buffer and reuse it when the next
mul_mat_vec_q has the same src1 tensor, data, shape and strides. The graph
loop invalidates it when any node writes the src1 memory, at every graph
evaluation and off the main stream. The buffer (4 MiB) is allocated
outside stream capture and kept until the context is freed, so captured
graphs stay valid. Disable with GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_Q8_1_REUSE.

R9700, Inkling-2-Mini Q4_K_M, with #400-#402 applied: tg128 47.6 -> 48.4
t/s, bitwise identical (KLD 0 with ubatch 16, 4 sequences). New
test-backend-ops case MUL_MAT_SHARED_SRC1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
