From b29d515403660f9f6aade5ab424258936473ad02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: paleluna82-del <260293746+paleluna82-del@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:20:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] inkling2 : fuse the one-query depth mix on CUDA/HIP

The depth mix (attention over the RMS-normalized earlier block outputs
with a learned query) was RMS_NORM -> RESHAPE -> CONCAT -> CONCAT ->
MUL_MAT -> SOFT_MAX -> MUL -> SUM_ROWS, 88 times per token. Fuse it into
one kernel per token that reads the stacked states and the current state
once (squares, scores), does the softmax in registers and writes the
weighted sum. The kernel reads the stack in its [E, n, T] layout only, so
the fusion checks that the transposed stack is built from the same
normalized states by the same concats. inkling2 expands the per-token
query repeat first so that the nodes stay adjacent for ubatches > 1.
Disable with GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_DEPTH_MIX_FUSION.

R9700, Inkling-2-Mini Q4_K_M, with #400-#402 applied: tg128 48.3 -> 50.8
t/s, pp512 1550 -> 1640. KLD vs unfused 0.0024 at ubatch 16 (rounding
from the reordered reductions; PPL c512 7.6899 -> 7.6851). New
test-backend-ops case DEPTH_MIX.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
